  {
   "_id": 11425,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"6911\" data-start=\"6808\">Effective integration ensures the GUI reflects backend computations dynamically. Example:</p>\n\n<p>from tkinter import *</p>\n\n<p>def calculate():<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; try:<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; result = eval(entry.get())<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; label.config(text=f&quot;Result: {result}&quot;)<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; except:<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; label.config(text=&quot;Invalid input&quot;)</p>\n\n<p>window = Tk()<br />\nentry = Entry(window)<br />\nentry.pack()<br />\nButton(window, text=&quot;Compute&quot;, command=calculate).pack()<br />\nlabel = Label(window, text=&quot;&quot;)<br />\nlabel.pack()<br />\nwindow.mainloop()<br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Here, user input is processed via backend (<code data-end=\"7333\" data-start=\"7325\">eval()</code>), and output is reflected in GUI. Evaluation shows how events act as the bridge between UI and logic.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 5,
